     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I am trying to specify a multitrait-multistate model (two states, six item-specific traits) in lavaan; I&#39;ve attached a diagram for illustration. Unfortunately, I am running into problems with negative ov and lv variances (i.e., warning messages &quot;some estimated ov/lv variances are negative&quot;), which I have not been able to resolve. The model looks as follows (I&#39;ve included code to simulate a data set. This does not always yield usable data; I have attached a data frame that yields the relevant error):</div><div><br></div><div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#800\"># GENERATE DATA</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>t </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\">times</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>s </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\">times</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">){</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> paste</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;y&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> times</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> each</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># MODEL</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sis </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;<br># latent variables<br>## latent states<br>s1 =~ 1*y11 + la211*y21 + la311*y31 + la411*y41 + la511*y51 + la611*y61<br>s2 =~ 1*y12 + la221*y22 + la321*y32 + la421*y42 + la521*y52 + la621*y62<br><br><br>## latent traits<br>t1 =~ 1*y11 + la122*y12<br>t2 =~ 1*y21 + la222*y22 <br>t3 =~ 1*y31 + la322*y32<br>t4 =~ 1*y41 + la422*y42<br>t5 =~ 1*y51 + la522*y52<br>t6 =~ 1*y61 + la622*y62<br><br><br># (co)variances<br>## variances of states s<br>s1 ~~ vars1*s1 <br>s2 ~~ vars2*s2 <br><br><br>## variances of traits t<br>t1 ~~ vart1*t1<br>t2 ~~ vart2*t2<br>t3 ~~ vart3*t3<br>t4 ~~ vart4*t4<br>t5 ~~ vart5*t5<br>t6 ~~ vart6*t6<br><br><br>## variances of indicators<br>y11 ~~ vary11*y11<br>y21 ~~ vary21*y21<br>y31 ~~ vary31*y31<br>y41 ~~ vary41*y41<br>y51 ~~ vary51*y51<br>y61 ~~ vary61*y61<br>y12 ~~ vary12*y12<br>y22 ~~ vary22*y22<br>y32 ~~ vary32*y32<br>y42 ~~ vary42*y42<br>y52 ~~ vary52*y52<br>y62 ~~ vary62*y62<br><br><br>## covariances<br>s1 + s2 ~~ 0*t1 + 0*t2 + 0*t3 + 0*t4 + 0*t5 + 0*t6 # covariances of states and traits set to 0<br>s1 ~~ 0*s2 # covariances of states set to 0<br>t1 ~~ cov12*t2 + cov13*t3 + cov14*t4 + cov15*t5 + cov16*t6<br>t2 ~~ cov23*t3 + cov24*t4 + cov25*t5 + cov26*t6<br>t3 ~~ cov34*t4 + cov35*t5 + cov36*t6<br>t4 ~~ cov45*t5 + cov46*t6<br>t5 ~~ cov56*t6<br><br><br># invariances<br><br><br>vars1 == vars2<br>&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># FIT CFA</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cfa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>I have tried to resolve this problem by specifying additional invariances between the factor loadings for the latent trait factors:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">la211 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> la221<br>la311 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> la321<br>la411 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> la421<br>la511 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> la521<br>la611 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> la621</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>However, this does not resolve the issue. At the moment, I am puzzled as to why the CFA leads to negative variances; so I&#39;d appreciate any pointers.</div><div><br></div><div>Kind regards,</div><div>Simon</div><div><br></div></div>"
